Intercept a dyn's result as a named construction, and resolve a bare slot type

Dev accepted the next related point after e241378, in these words: "route a dyn's result
(body `fix value` and leaf) through constructionInitializer with the existing expression
fallback, re-author Observable's `_geocentric:` as `geocentric:` with its JSON re-canonicalized
and Scala byte-identical, and add one NamedConstructionTest case." Until now a dyn's RESULT
rendered through the plain expression, so a named argument reached Scala without the factory's
`_` prefix, and world/Observable's fromGeodetic authored `_geocentric:` by hand — a Scala
spelling inside a drake source. Measured before building: 86 `fix value` results in the corpus,
one of them a named construction (Observable's); six Text-typed with non-literal values, four of
those plain paths (`rendered.value`, `line.value`, `_compound.value`), which rules out routing a
result through the full initializer, whose String-slot rule would quote them. So the route is
the narrow one: a new `dynResult` helper, `constructionInitializer(valueType, value)` with
`expression(value)` as the fallback, at all five result sites — resultOf's body `value`, the
leaf dyn in typeBody, and the two methodBody callers.

ONE ENABLING CHANGE beyond the accepted words, flagged to Dev with the gate: the first probe
left Observable unmapped, because loadDracoType looked up only a DOTTED slot type and the result
is `fix value Observable` — Input had worked only by spelling its slot type qualified. The
generator now keeps `definitionInEffect`, a lazy thread-local set by generateSpelled while a
definition is spelled (the body moved to `spelledSource`), and a bare slot type resolves against
that definition's package, exactly as namesCodecless resolves a bare parameter type. Without it
Observable's Scala could not stay byte-identical with `geocentric:` authored; with it, unscoped
and scoped generation agree, since canonical spelling already qualified such names under a
scope. No definition in effect leaves a bare name unresolved as before.

Observable.drake authors `geocentric:`; its JSON was re-canonicalized with the compiled parser and
differs in that one leaf. Observable.scala regenerates byte-identical, as do Input, Output and
Consumer, so no committed Scala moves. NamedConstructionTest gains the accepted case — a probe
whose named construction is a body result and a leaf result, both generated, compiled and run —
and its own-package case now authors the slot type bare, pinning the resolution above.
The remaining observation stays preserved and unaccepted: the interception keys its factory
lookup on the slot type rather than the applied head.

